## Fumadocs Patterns

### Content Sourcing

- Content lives in repo root `docs/`. The site sources from `../docs` via `site/source.config.ts`.
- `docs/standards/` is excluded from Fumadocs — it does not render as documentation pages.
- Every directory that appears in the sidebar needs a `meta.json` for ordering and an `index.mdx` as the section landing page.

### `meta.json` Files

Each docs subdirectory uses a `meta.json` to control sidebar ordering:

```json
{
  "title": "Section Title",
  "pages": ["page-one", "page-two", "page-three"]
}
```

The `pages` array controls display order. Entries are file slugs without extensions.

### Index Pages

Every sidebar section has an `index.mdx` that serves as the section landing page:
- Brief description of what the section covers.
- Card links to the most important pages.
- "Coming Soon" indicator for planned but unwritten pages.

### MDX Files

- Use `.mdx` extension for all new documentation (not `.md`).
- MDX supports JSX components — but keep usage minimal. Prefer standard Markdown.
- Fumadocs renders Mermaid code blocks natively.

### URL Slugs

- Lowercase with hyphens: `agent-execution-lifecycle`, not `AgentExecutionLifecycle`.
- Resource name for concept docs: `agent.mdx`, `skill.mdx`, `mcp-server.mdx`.
- Command or topic name for CLI docs: `configuration.mdx`, `managing-agents.mdx`.
- Descriptive action phrases for guides: `deploying-with-apply.mdx`, `using-mcp-servers.mdx`.

### Static Export

- The site uses `output: "export"` — every page must have `generateStaticParams`.
- Build with Node.js 20 LTS (`nvm use 20`). Node 23 causes silent webpack crashes.
- Turbopack is disabled — external `../docs/` resolution requires webpack.

---

## Cross-Referencing

- Use relative links: `[What is an Agent?](../concepts/agent.mdx)`.
- Link to the canonical document for a concept — never duplicate explanations.
- Anchor links must point to actual headings.

---

## Diagrams

- Use Mermaid for flowcharts, sequence diagrams, architecture diagrams.
- Use ASCII art only for simple inline diagrams that do not benefit from Mermaid.
- Every diagram must have surrounding text that conveys the same information.

